{
  "_comment": "Adds 2026-09-12 — gear people typed on their lists (catalog_candidates, scanned 2026-09-12: 497 open rows / 458 keys, 190 new since the 09-02 pass) that the catalog was missing, graduated to cited rows from each maker's own page. Two lists drove most of it: a UK hiker (Alpkit Koro, and a Terra Nova tent and Petzl headtorch typed without a model, so not added) and a Japan/Montbell-heavy one — 'Montbell Bear' at 19 g worn is a trekking bell, so the maker's bells are here at the maker's figures (36/90/44 g; the plain Round bell weighs the same as the Monta Bear one, so only the printed edition the list named is kept); 'Montbell Thermawrap Jacket' names a family, so the family's jackets and parkas are here. Montbell pages print one weight and no size, so those rows record size as unpublished. Ortovox prints 64 g and 62 g for the women's Sport Top and Hot Pants (the list carried 84/92 — the men's boxer's figure), REI's current-season Merino 185 pages print no weight but the prior listings still do (5.6 oz size M women's, 7.4 oz size L men's). Nothing's Ear (open) — the parenthetical is its version, so it is the row's variant — follows the Powerbeats ruling: carried is the case plus both buds, 63.8 + 2 × 8.1 = 80.0 g. Sambob's own store lists the Alpha 60 and Alpha 90 crewnecks at approximate weights (~2.5 oz, ~3.5 oz) with no size. Food follows the KIND/Clif convention (label weight per bar from the nutrition panel, calories from the same panel); the Olyra panel is an image on the maker's page, transcribed; the Trader Joe's tuna pouch is sourced at net contents and says so. Dropped, no maker weight anywhere: Verve Craft Instant (only a per-cup 5 g dose), Quinn, Smelly Proof, Ursa Major wipes, Dooy (Amazon brand, reviewer-measured only); ic! berlin sits behind a Cloudflare human check. The Garmin and Mountain Hardwear candidates (inReach Mini 3 Plus, fēnix, Rockrydge Pant) are in this PR's garmin and mountain-hardwear files instead.",
